  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "All electromagnetic wave is transporting energy in the negative <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math> direction. At a certain point and certain time the direction of electric field of the wave is along positive <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math> direction. What will be the direction of the magnetic field of the wave at that point and instant?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "0c71a",
      "text": "Positive direction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Hj95b",
      "text": "Positive direction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ALSiK",
      "text": "Negative direction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Kq7c8",
      "text": "Negative direction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In an electromagnetic wave, the direction of energy flow is along the direction of the wave propagation. Therefore, the wave propagates along negative z direction.&nbsp;</p><p>Electric field is along the positive y direction and the wave propagates along negative z direction. Thus, magnetic&nbsp;field is in&nbsp;direction perpendicular to both z&nbsp;and y axes.&nbsp;</p><p>Using vector algebra,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mfenced></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;magnetic field is in positive <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> direction.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
